-- CHEMICAL REACTION ENGINEERING & THERMODYNAMICS | Mid 1 | easy | 460009382502011
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers") VALUES (460009382502011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain and apply Scope and importance of chemical reaction engineering in “Introduction to Chemical Reaction Engineering”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Batch in “Types of Reactors & Characteristics”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Rate equation/ Rate law in “Kinetics of Homogeneous Reactions”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Introduction & Basic concept of thermodynamics in “Introduction & Basic concept of thermodynamics”; include the governing principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Scope and importance of chemical reaction engineering is covered in “Introduction to Chemical Reaction Engineering”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Classification of chemical reactions (Homogeneous vs. Heterogeneous, Catalytic vs. Non-catalytic, Reversible vs. Irreversible, By Molecularity, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Classification of chemical reactions (Homogeneous vs. Heterogeneous, Catalytic vs. Non-catalytic, Reversible vs. Irreversible, By Molecularity.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic CHEMICAL REACTION ENGINEERING & THERMODYNAMICS task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Batch is covered in “Types of Reactors & Characteristics”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Semi-Batch, Continuous stirred tank reactor, Tubular, Multiphase, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Semi-Batch, Continuous stirred tank reactor, Tubular, Multiphase.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic CHEMICAL REACTION ENGINEERING & THERMODYNAMICS task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Rate equation/ Rate law is covered in “Kinetics of Homogeneous Reactions”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Concentration dependent term of rate (Equation, Rate constant, Elementary and non-elementary reactions), Molecularity and order of reaction., give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Concentration dependent term of rate (Equation, Rate constant, Elementary and non-elementary reactions), Molecularity and order of reaction..\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic CHEMICAL REACTION ENGINEERING & THERMODYNAMICS task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Introduction & Basic concept of thermodynamics is covered in “Introduction & Basic concept of thermodynamics”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Introduction & Basic concept of thermodynamics, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Introduction & Basic concept of thermodynamics.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic CHEMICAL REACTION ENGINEERING & THERMODYNAMICS task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

