nnect it to Various types of rubber, Applications and Manufacturing of: Ethylene Propylene Terpolymers Butyl rubber Polyurethane, Silicone rubber, Rubbers.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Nylon-6 and Nylon 6 6 and their difference is covered in “Processing of polymers”. Define it, describe the main steps/components, relate it to Mastication, Mixing, Moulding, Extrusion, give an example and mention a check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Mastication, Mixing, Moulding, Extrusion.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Polymerization converts monomers into polymers; conditions affect molecular weight, structure and properties.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Polymerization, Solution polymerization. Suspension polymerization, Emulsion polymerization. Molecular weight, Crystallinity and Glass transition temperature. Properties of Plastics: Electrical Resistance.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply it to a realistic POLYMER TECHNOLOGY task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention a relevant limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

